{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QuantumObservableUniverses.CategoricalQLieBracket","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QuantumObservableUniverses.CategoricalQLieBracket","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Monoidal.Category","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Category.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Preadditive.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Linear.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Laurent","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Int.Basic"],"declarations":15,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalQLieBracket.q_bracket_classical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalQLieBracket.q_bracket_classical","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-q-lie-bracket.lean#L79-L89","doc":"At `q = 1`, the q-bracket reduces to the classical bracket. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalQLieBracket.q_bracket","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalQLieBracket.q_bracket","kind":"def","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-q-lie-bracket.lean#L67-L77","doc":"The q-deformed bracket evaluated on two derivations.\n\n`[X, Y]_q = q⁻¹ · [X, Y] + (1 − q⁻¹) · (θ(X) · [ξ, Y] − θ(Y) · [ξ, X])`\n\nIn a preadditive ℝ-linear category, this is a well-defined endomorphism. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalQLieBracket.q_unit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalQLieBracket.q_unit","kind":"theorem","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-q-lie-bracket.lean#L65-L65","doc":"`q` is a unit: `q · q⁻¹ = 1` (`qinv` + `q_unit` encode `q⁻¹`\nwithout needing an `Inv` instance on the Laurent ring `R_q`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalQLieBracket.qinv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalQLieBracket.qinv","kind":"def","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-q-lie-bracket.lean#L62-L62","doc":"The inverse `q⁻¹ ∈ R_q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalQLieBracket.q_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalQLieBracket.q_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-q-lie-bracket.lean#L60-L60","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalQLieBracket.q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalQLieBracket.q","kind":"def","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-q-lie-bracket.lean#L59-L59","doc":"The deformation parameter `q`, non-zero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalQLieBracket.theta","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalQLieBracket.theta","kind":"def","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-q-lie-bracket.lean#L57-L57","doc":"The canonical 1-form `θ_A : A → 𝟙`, dual to `ξ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalQLieBracket.xi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalQLieBracket.xi","kind":"def","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-q-lie-bracket.lean#L55-L55","doc":"The Reeb derivation `ξ : A → A`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalQLieBracket.bracket","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalQLieBracket.bracket","kind":"def","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-q-lie-bracket.lean#L53-L53","doc":"The classical Lie bracket `[−, −] : End(A) × End(A) → End(A)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalQLieBracket.A","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalQLieBracket.A","kind":"def","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-q-lie-bracket.lean#L51-L51","doc":"The Frobenius–Hopf object `A`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalQLieBracket.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalQLieBracket.mk","kind":"ctor","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-q-lie-bracket.lean#L48-L48","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.CategoricalQLieBracket","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.CategoricalQLieBracket","kind":"structure","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-q-lie-bracket.lean#L38-L65","doc":"**Categorical q-Lie bracket**.\n\nOn derivations of the Frobenius–Hopf object `A`, the `q`-deformed Lie\nbracket is defined by:\n`[X, Y]_q = q⁻¹ [X, Y] + (1 − q⁻¹)(θ_A(X) [ξ, Y] − θ_A(Y) [ξ, X])`\n\nAt `q = 1`, this recovers the classical commutator.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{def:categorical-q-lie-bracket}`\nRef: [lusztig1993] https://doi.org/10.1007/978-0-8176-4717-9 ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:categorical-q-lie-bracket","label":"def:categorical-q-lie-bracket","md":"quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-q-lie-bracket.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.q_inv_param","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.q_inv_param","kind":"def","line":34,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-q-lie-bracket.lean#L34-L34","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.q_param","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.q_param","kind":"def","line":33,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-q-lie-bracket.lean#L33-L33","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.R_q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.R_q","kind":"def","line":30,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/categorical-q-lie-bracket.lean#L30-L32","doc":"Ground ring `R_q = ℤ[q, q⁻¹]` (Laurent polynomials over ℤ).\nSee `QOU.Archimedean.GroundRing` for the compiled definition. ","signatureChunk":0}]}